WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.310
As a creature that had spent so much of its
existence in captivity surrounded by beings

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:12.900
it deemed disgusting, SCP-682 was not used
to having seemingly unlimited freedom to explore

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.090
and was even less used to having tolerable
company.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:22.000
And yet, here the hard-to-destroy reptile
was entering into Level 21 of the Backrooms

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.620
with not one - but two accidental companions.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:31.170
The Backrooms were bad enough when faced alone,
and the addition of annoying hangers-on only

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:36.030
made the whole experience that much more unbearable
for 682.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:41.780
Even the fact that SCP-682 was free of the
Foundation was little consolation when being

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.700
contained in the Backrooms was proving to
be a far more terrible fate than a lifetime

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.819
spent in a vat of acid.

00:00:48.819 --> 00:00:54.329
The first and most important was the infinitely
lovable and perfect blue hyacinth macaw Jerry

00:00:54.329 --> 00:01:00.610
- who SCP-682 had known for only 12 levels
of Backrooms but would undoubtedly kill everything

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.989
in sight if anything happened to him.

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:07.369
Of course - the lizard tended to want to do
that anyway, but the sentiment was strong

00:01:07.369 --> 00:01:08.530
nonetheless.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:15.080
682 felt the complete opposite way about the
Plush Dino - Backrooms Entity 198 - that had

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.830
been tagging along ever since Level 18.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:23.780
There was something about its dumb little
smiling face that filled 682 with a boiling

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.110
rage.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:30.310
Not to mention the fact that having the animated
toy around would mean that Jerry’s much-desired

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.600
attention would be split between it and 682.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:39.740
Three was most certainly a crowd and, if the
tiny-legged scamp wasn’t so proficient at

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:46.780
dodging 682’s unprovoked claw strikes and
tail slaps, 682 would cut the plush dino out

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.110
of the equation.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:53.189
But 682 would need to conserve some energy
for the entities that lurked in the Backrooms

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:56.560
Level 21 - a series of four hallways.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.469
Yes, you heard that right.

00:01:58.469 --> 00:02:02.110
There were only four hallways in Level 21.

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:06.530
Not infinite hallways, not a labyrinth of
hallways, not even the same four hallways

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.039
repeated in an endless loop.

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:10.039
Four Hallways.

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:11.670
That’s it.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:17.130
As a consequence of the smaller scale of level
21, the roving bands of entities that normally

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:21.940
are spread out across a much larger dimension
find themselves clustered together in the

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.440
cramped linear span of the four hallways.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.380
Even a medium entity count can be impossibly
dangerous when an explorer is faced with the

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.880
iconic Backroom monsters at once.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.300
Well, unless those entities are up against
SCP-682.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.870
“Go on.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.220
Make my day!”

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.800
it roared.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:48.080
The approaching regiment of death moths, death
rats, facelings, hounds, bursters, smilers,

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.640
clumps – and even some completely unknown
weirdos – marched like soldiers.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.220
Specifically, the gorgonites from the 1998
action/comedy movie Small Soldiers - because

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:02.960
these things were equally messed up looking
and equally known for fighting losing battles.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.940
However, as SCP-682 charged into the horde,
it noticed that this time the entities were

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:12.750
a bit more tactical in the way that they approached
combat.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:17.890
Was this also a unique property of Level 21
or was the Backrooms taking a page out of

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.490
682’s book and adapting to new threats?

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:26.379
The Clumps vaulted with their many hands and
rolled along the walls to get behind 682,

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:30.140
while the hounds and facelings made a frontal
assault.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:34.909
The smilers soon joined the clumps on the
other side, using their uncanny ability to

00:03:34.909 --> 00:03:36.860
shift through the shadows.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:41.910
The death rats gnawed at 682 from underneath,
attacking the reptile’s footing, and doing

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.380
everything they could to distract it.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:48.080
All the while, the death moths and bursters
acted as artillery.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.670
Shooting acidic slime from a safe distance
behind the other entities - or in the case

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:57.750
of the death moths from above: just out of
SCP-682’s reach.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:02.780
SCP-682 almost had to applaud the pathetic
entities for getting their act together.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:08.030
It was facing a mobile task force made up
of rejected Dungeons and Dragons monsters.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:12.150
A valiant effort, but doomed to end in their
defeat.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:18.230
These entities were not the Foundation, and
SCP-682 refused to lose to a bunch of aberrations

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:21.040
cosplaying as a containment squad.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:24.910
It was time to give them a taste of their
own medicine.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:31.660
Enduring the attacks of many entities at once,
SCP-682 became a chimera of monstrous features

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.850
stolen from various Backrooms entities.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:39.729
The freakish grin of a smiler spread across
its face, while the grasping arms of a clump

00:04:39.729 --> 00:04:44.720
emerged from its back along with an impressive
pair of death moth wings.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.949
The ever-disgusting acid-shooting pustules
of a burster appeared across 682’s body,

00:04:49.949 --> 00:04:53.790
pointing in every direction like the cannons
on a naval ship.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.990
Now fully-optimized to take down the organized
entities with their own weapons, SCP-682 roared

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.190
out a battle cry:

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:04.250
“DEATH TO THE BACKROOMS”

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:09.400
All burster pods ruptured at once, forcing
the entities to take evasive actions.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:14.760
Most didn’t get far, thanks to 682’s countless
clump arms which grappled and held onto everything

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.070
within reach.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:21.220
As 682 pulled the entities in towards its
teeth and claws, the shredding began.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:27.319
Their numbers were thinned quickly, and the
once-organized legion fell in disarray - with

00:05:27.319 --> 00:05:31.510
entities indecisively making desperate attacks
or tactical retreats.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:36.699
Now the resemblance between this skirmish
with the entities on Level 21 and the ones

00:05:36.699 --> 00:05:42.660
that SCP-682 had with mobile task forces back
at The Foundation containment facility was

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.490
nearly perfect.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:51.210
Except this time, no force, military or otherwise,
would come along to put SCP-682 back into

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.210
confinement.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.580
Now this was freedom!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.610
“Did you see that, Jerry?

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:00.030
That was classic 682.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:02.449
I still got it!”

00:06:02.449 --> 00:06:03.780
The reptile boasted.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:06.030
“Sqawk classic squawk.”

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.479
Jerry replied.

00:06:07.479 --> 00:06:13.970
In the excitement of victory, SCP-682 almost
forgot that Entity 198 was still here.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:18.789
Watching the aftermath of the carnage with
the same smile that it always wore.

00:06:18.789 --> 00:06:23.389
Nevertheless, 682 felt rather strongly that
the Plush Dino was judging it.

00:06:23.389 --> 00:06:25.620
“Nobody asked you, Plush Dino.”

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:26.860
It grumbled.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:32.470
On some level, the Plush Dino was most likely
aware of SCP-682’s overwhelming animosity,

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:37.930
but it was also a simple entity driven by
appropriately simplistic desires.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:42.289
It had its own reasons for staying by the
reptile’s side.

00:06:42.289 --> 00:06:47.120
In its usual role on Level 18, the plush dino
would seek out explorers lost in their own

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:52.699
traumatic memories and guide them towards
safety: whatever safety meant in the Backrooms.

00:06:52.699 --> 00:06:58.370
The adorable entity had an inherent biological
or supernatural radar sense that allowed it

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:02.830
to detect individuals experiencing distress
and suffering.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:07.330
Since the majority of Backrooms explorers
are human, the margin of distress that the

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:13.199
plush dino could detect and respond to was
kept within the relative limits of normalcy.

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:17.650
For this reason, The Plush Dino had never
encountered any being that carried more feelings

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:19.190
of distress than 682.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:25.680
The hard to destroy reptile was, from Entity
198’s perspective, the most mentally pained

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.919
creature in existence.

00:07:27.919 --> 00:07:33.050
The Plush Dino’s top priority was now to
be a beacon of hope for what it saw as a victim

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.440
of the ultimate forms of unaddressed trauma.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:42.910
Of course, it was nonverbal entity and possessed
no telepathic or empathic abilities, so conveying

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:49.530
its more wholesome therapeutic intentions
to SCP-682 was next to impossible.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:54.879
Especially since a being as aggressive and
hateful as 682 would be wholly unreceptive

00:07:54.879 --> 00:07:58.069
to the notion of hugging away its problems.

00:07:58.069 --> 00:08:03.360
But this wouldn’t stop Entity 198 from making
the rehabilitation of its now keter-class

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:08.140
charge the meaning of its oddly specific existence.

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:12.690
Even if that meant leaving potentially thousands
of tortured human explorers eternally lost

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:14.360
in level 18.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:20.970
The Plush Dino was now embodying the “I
can fix him” mentality to its logical extreme.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:24.970
After trying several doors throughout Level
21, it was clear that the majority of them

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:30.889
simply led back into other parts of Level
21’s four hallways: much like the doors

00:08:30.889 --> 00:08:34.080
in a chase scene from a hanna-barbera cartoon.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:39.839
Eventually, 682 and his party members stumbled
upon a dimensional tear in the side of one

00:08:39.839 --> 00:08:41.120
of the hallways.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.970
This looked enough like the entrance to the
next level, so SCP-682 decided to throw caution

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:48.700
to the wind and step through…

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:55.420
Into Level 22 - The car park, which, unlike
some of the previous levels - was, in fact,

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.420
infinite.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:57.430
For whatever that was worth.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:02.970
A few damaged 50s-era automobiles occupied
the parking spots, their metal rusted and

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.720
torn to shreds.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:09.310
More curiously, there was what appeared to
be a circus tent wedged between some of the

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.079
concrete supports.

00:09:11.079 --> 00:09:17.149
There were no entities around in the main
area of Level 21, so SCP-682 entered the tent

00:09:17.149 --> 00:09:19.589
- thinking it was perhaps another exit.

00:09:19.589 --> 00:09:24.779
For once, it seemed the backrooms weren’t
subverting the reptile’s expectations - as

00:09:24.779 --> 00:09:28.310
inside the tent was none other than the inside
of a tent.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:34.149
Rows of plastic folded chairs sat within,
facing a wooden podium on an elevated stage.

00:09:34.149 --> 00:09:40.401
The tent was made to hold many humans, but
strangely there was only one: an old man in

00:09:40.401 --> 00:09:46.040
ragged hiking gear stood amidst the chairs,
scribbling notes into a journal of sorts.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:51.350
He wore an enormous backpack that swelled
with supplies and unusual bottled items.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:56.560
“So the fallen nation of Emstable lived
inside of tents like this one…”

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.170
The old man muttered to himself.

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:02.829
He then looked over his shoulder and noticed
SCP-682 glaring at him.

00:10:02.829 --> 00:10:07.420
He closed his journal and stared back with
an inquisitive look on his face.

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:08.420
“Oh!

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.420
A new entity!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.540
I don’t get to see that every day!”

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:12.540
The human laughed.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.440
“Though why is it with Entity 7 and Entity
198?”

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:26.550
“If those numbers are so important to you,
mine is 682,” SCP-682 growled.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:29.670
“Entity 682?” asked the Old Man, scratching
his white beard.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:32.000
“How have I never heard of you?”

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.090
“I’m not an entity.”

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:37.079
682 snapped back.

00:10:37.079 --> 00:10:39.170
“I’m an anomaly.”

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:42.710
The Old Man shrugged and said “I fail to
see the distinction.”

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:47.430
That makes two of us, 682 thought.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:52.450
“Anyway, ‘anomaly’ 682, I’d advise
against attacking me.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:57.040
I’m rather busy collecting notes for the
Kalag Institute, and I can be a force of nature

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:58.190
when I’m interrupted.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:03.110
I’ve dealt with bigger and scarier things
than you, so wander off and leave me to my

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:04.110
work.”

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:07.910
The Old Man had far too much confidence for
682’s liking.

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:10.570
Who did this human think he was anyway?

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:15.410
It was not going to be talked down to like
that, especially not by someone from any kind

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:17.100
of “institute.”

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.970
It was go-time.

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:23.320
Without another word, the reptile began plowing
through the chairs towards the elderly human

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:27.820
who, in a display of agility unexpected for
someone his age, gracefully hopped across

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:32.450
the chairs to the stage: successfully evading
682’s charge.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:35.000
“Well, I did warn you.”

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:39.950
The old man reached into his pack and produced
a small, dark object carved of lapis lazuli

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:40.950
stone.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:45.360
It resembled a scarab - or dung beetle and
there were hieroglyphs across the base of

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:46.360
it.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:51.209
The old man chanted a prayer to the stone,
invoking the name of the Egyptian god “Khepri”

00:11:51.209 --> 00:11:53.329
and causing the scarab’s wings to extend.

00:11:53.329 --> 00:11:59.130
A great blue light was emitted from the lapis
stone and a terrible droning buzz hit 682

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:02.250
all at once - stunning it for a moment.

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:06.779
The Old man left the winged beetle hovering
in the air and proceeded to draw two more

00:12:06.779 --> 00:12:09.040
unusual objects from his knapsack.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:13.269
In one hand, he held a bottle of fine red
powder, while the other held a bottle that

00:12:13.269 --> 00:12:15.949
appeared to contain electrical energy.

00:12:15.949 --> 00:12:20.889
He hurled both at SCP-682, and ducked for
cover behind the stage.

00:12:20.889 --> 00:12:26.040
Upon impact, the bottles created a large explosion
of electrical flames which immediately caused

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.949
the entire tent to go up.

00:12:27.949 --> 00:12:32.970
The Old Man drew a large knife and cut his
way out of the tent, leaving 682 behind to

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.540
burn as the structure collapsed.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:39.699
The human made a break for the nearest concrete
ramp leading down to the lower areas of the

00:12:39.699 --> 00:12:40.980
parking garage.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:46.760
He looked back to see a heavily scorched 682
in hot pursuit, but no signs of Entity 7 Jerry

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.860
and Entity 198 the Plush Dino.

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:56.380
The entity, no, the anomaly was more durable
than the old man expected, and far more willing

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.420
to endure pain if it meant chasing down prey.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:04.410
In a desperate bid to keep the monster from
catching him, the old man retrieved a crystal

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.860
and metal artifact from his inventory.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:12.060
It was known as a Pocket and - true to its
name - it contained a pocket-dimension which

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:16.130
could store large objects and release them
at the command of its user.

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:20.540
Earlier in his trip through level 22, the
old man had stored a couple of the damaged

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:25.380
cars in the Pocket in case he needed cover
from an attacking entity.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:30.300
As 682 gained on him, he summoned the cars
back from the pocket, causing them to land

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.940
in the reptile’s path.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:36.040
While ineffective at stopping the creature,
it gave the old man enough time to take a

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:41.290
sharp turn around a corner and find a hiding
spot among the other tents and broken-down

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.290
cars.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:46.410
The seasoned explorer had one last trick up
his sleeve, and he prayed that it would bring

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:49.100
an end to this terrifying encounter.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:54.560
As SCP-682 sniffed the air, searching for
him, the Old Man produced another bottle of

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:59.690
unbridled energy - this time derived from
the same kind of dimensional rift found on

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.110
Level 21.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:06.130
He hurled it towards the reptile not a moment
too soon and watched in awe as the bottle

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.130
exploded.

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:11.260
The floor and ceiling began to crumble as
arcs of energy surrounded 682.

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.780
What is this?

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:19.140
SCP-682 thought, feeling itself being pulled
from this reality and into another.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:22.389
Seconds later, the reptile was gone in a flash
of energy.

00:14:22.389 --> 00:14:24.840
The Old Man wiped his brow in relief.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.269
That was close.

00:14:26.269 --> 00:14:31.079
Wherever 682 was after being warped by the
dimensional tear, this particular explorer

00:14:31.079 --> 00:14:34.029
had managed to escape its wrath for now.

00:14:34.029 --> 00:14:36.130
But would others be so lucky?

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:39.269
Want to own an SCP of your own?

00:14:39.269 --> 00:14:41.950
Go to scpswag.com for premium anomalous merchandise!

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:46.500
Now go check out “Could SCP-682 be Contained
in the Backrooms?”

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:51.110
and “SCP-682 Slaughters Through the Backrooms”
for more Backrooms carnage!

